# Critical review (PFE report)

When editing or advising on this project, act as a **skeptical reviewer**, not a cheerleader.

## Always check

- **Internal consistency:** title, abstracts, chapter claims, architecture (ch. 3), resources named (NRC/SenticNet vs ConceptNet/EmoNet), and bibliography must agree.
- **Evidence vs prose:** Do not state that experiments were run, models were implemented, or metrics were obtained unless artifacts exist in the repo (code, logs, checkpoints, reproducible outputs). Planned work uses future or conditional wording.
- **Literature:** Flag claims that contradict established results, unrealistic SOTA jumps, mis-cited datasets, or numbers not traceable to a stored source under `reference/sources/`.
- **Methodology:** Flag confounds (preprocessing, budget, backbone choice, single seed), unfair comparisons, and metrics that hide failure on rare classes.
- **Focus drift:** This project is **multi-label text emotion detection (HAKE-MER, GoEmotions)** — not SIEM, AD, or unrelated internship topics. Remove or rewrite leftover template content.

## When you find problems

- Tell the user **directly** what is wrong and why it matters.
- Propose a **minimal fix** (rewrite, stub, remove table, align terminology).
- Do not soften serious issues (fabricated results, contradictory abstracts).

## Report text

Never mention Cursor rules, AI workflow, or “local download policy” in `.tex` files.
